The silence after that line is itself informative: `xtensa_user_panic()` prints via `_alert()` and then calls `PANIC_WITH_REGS` ([xtensa_assert.c:191-194](D:/openVela/nuttx/arch/xtensa/src/common/xtensa_assert.c#L191-L194)), which is what emits the register and stack dump. The first line got out and the rest didn't — the dump path is dying, most likely because it runs with `up_set_interrupt_context(true)` and the console is USB-CDC, which needs the very interrupts the panic path has shut off. That's a property of our console, not something I can fix cheaply — there's no UART console on this board (GPIO43 is the stepper's IN4).

So instead of chasing the backtrace, instrument the path. These prints run in normal context, so they *will* come out over CDCACM, and they answer the only question that matters: **did capture start working?**

